# =============================================================================
# Docker build-context exclusions.
#
# The repo root is the build context for docker/Dockerfile.clio-* (the TUI
# build needs the go.work workspace, so the context cannot be narrowed to a
# single dir). Without this file the context is multiple GB — research clones,
# node_modules, Go/Rust/Vite build outputs, screenshots, and GIFs. Keep this
# list aggressive: only the source the Dockerfiles actually COPY needs to be
# present.
# =============================================================================

# --- VCS / CI / editor ---
.git
.github
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.mcp.json
.playwright-mcp
.claude
.tools

# --- Read-only research clones (huge) ---
research
apps/research
apps/web/research

# --- Node / pnpm ---
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store
**/.vite
**/.turbo

# --- Python virtualenvs / caches ---
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.clio_agent
.clio-agent-artifacts

# --- Rust / Tauri build output (desktop app — not used by Docker) ---
apps/desktop/src-tauri/target
**/target

# --- Go build output ---
tui/gact
tui/gact.exe
emulator/emulator-server
**/*.test
**/*.exe

# --- Frontend build output (rebuilt inside the image) ---
apps/web/dist
apps/core/dist
**/dist
**/build

# --- Visual artifacts (never needed in an image) ---
screenshots
apps/web/screenshots
examples/loop-test
**/*.png
**/*.gif
**/*.tape
tmp

# --- Docs / planning (not needed at build time) ---
# NOTE: *.md is matched only at the repo root via the leading slash so that
# docker/*.conf / *.sh stay in context; docker/README.md is excluded below.
/*.md
notes
docs

# --- Docker scaffolding ---
# The Dockerfiles themselves are passed via -f and need not be in context, but
# docker/nginx-*.conf and docker/*-entrypoint.sh ARE COPYed by the web/tui
# images — so keep docker/ in the context and only drop what's build-irrelevant.
docker/Dockerfile.*
docker/README.md
docker/docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
